Nodes Specification:
If any one of the VMs were to fail, what happens to another's service? It wont work, so failure points should be made in Milestone 4.
- Have minimum 3 nodes/points of failure for DB, Msg/RMQ and 2 nodes for FE and BE
- Each extra node should not be on the same system/machine. 
    - Ex. If DB has one node, the other 2 nodes should not be on that machine, has to be somewhere else. Pick and choose where to allocate nodes.
-        No matter where the nodes are, the DB is responsible for those nodes, aka someone else hosting DB's nodes is not responsible for them.
    - Does not have to be on the same VM or it could. A separate VM can be made and non-master nodes can be used on that. 
- The VM/system/master-node itself counts as a node but the dependency on that master-node requires the building of failure points

- Composer Script Specs: "Your VM is a datacenter where it can shut down all or a few nodes."
    - The script needs to cater towards the environment aka nodes (needs to know where the nodes are, etc.)

**The nodes physically have to be on different VMs, not just 1 computer and 2 VMs  || Second node/non-master node should not be on the same system/VM

Additional features are to be expected but that depends on the bandwidth/viability of each group's progress

